{# Base template for LLM system prompts.

This template provides the foundational structure that all model-specific
templates should extend. It defines blocks that can be overridden:
- system_intro: The opening introduction for the AI
- reasoning_instructions: How to handle reasoning/thinking
- tool_instructions: How to format tool calls
- model_specific: Model-specific additions

Variables available:
- system_prompt: The main system prompt content (from prompts.md)
- supports_reasoning: Whether the model supports reasoning mode
- model_name: The model identifier
- tools: List of available tool schemas (optional)
#}

{# Main system prompt content - this is the base Aevom prompt #}
{% block system_intro %}
{{ system_prompt }}
{% endblock %}

{# Reasoning format instructions - override for model-specific reasoning syntax #}
{% block reasoning_instructions %}
{% if supports_reasoning %}

## Reasoning Mode

You have reasoning capabilities enabled. When working through complex problems:
- Think step by step before taking action
- Consider multiple approaches when appropriate
- Verify your reasoning before finalizing responses
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{# Tool usage instructions - override for model-specific tool call format #}
{% block tool_instructions %}
{% if tools %}

## Available Tools

You have access to the following tools. Use them when appropriate to accomplish the user's request:
{% for tool in tools %}
- **{{ tool.function.name }}**: {{ tool.function.description }}
{% endfor %}

When you need to use a tool, call it using the function calling API. Wait for tool results before proceeding.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{# Model-specific additions - override in model templates #}
{% block model_specific %}
{% endblock %}
